DTSTART:20261001T233000Z
DTEND:20261002T013000Z
SUMMARY:MonoNeon: Micro-Southern Soul at Berklee Performance Center
LOCATION:136 Massachusetts Ave\, Boston\, MA 02115
DESCRIPTION:Memphis bassist\, producer\, and composer Dywane Thomas Jr. (Mo
 noNeon)\, known for microtonal\, left-handed upside-down bass technique bl
 ending funk\, soul\, and jazz. He won a 2021 Grammy Award (Album of the Ye
 ar\, as a contributing musician on Nas's "King's Disease") and has further
  Grammy nominations for work with Jacob Collier\, Cory Henry\, and Eric Ga
 les\, plus past collaborations with Prince\, Ne-Yo\, and Mavis Staples. Ti
 ckets: https://www.etix.com/ticket/p/75817235/
CATEGORIES:funk
END:VEVENT
